<title>FINLAND: ASKO TO SELL SPORT GOODS UNITS TO BERNER.</title>
<headline>ASKO TO SELL SPORT GOODS UNITS TO BERNER.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Plastic pipes, furniture and white goods maker Asko Oy said in a statement on Friday its Karhu-Sport Oy unit will sell some businesses to privately owned Berner Oy.</p>
<p>The 1996 net sales of the units to be sold will be about 13 million markka, Asko said.  </p>
<p>Berner will acquire the Karhu-Sport unit that makes baseball bats and equipment for indoor bandy. The parties agreed on a long-term licensing deal about the use of the Karhu name on these products.</p>
<p>The divestment is part of Asko's strategy of streamlining its operations to focus on core businesses.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
